  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\nUpper trough will linger across central Canada through the next\nweek with an upper ridge over the Rockies. Various shortwaves will\nbe moving through the ridge over the next week, gradually\nflattening out the ridge. Over time this will bring cooler\ntemperatures and scattered showers. \n\nTomorrow will see a slight jump in temperatures along with\nstronger winds as a low pressure system moves across southern \nMontana. This also leads into critical fire conditions for the \nsouthwest fire zones. A Red Flag Warning has replaced the Fire\nWeather Watch, and additional zones have been included, but\ntiming remains the same. The window with the most critical \nconditions will be tomorrow from noon to 8 PM.\n\nAs the upper ridge flattens, and flow turns zonal, smoke will\nlikely return to northeast Montana for next week. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nIncreased winds using FV3, and continued using HRRR for day 1-3 \nsmoke. Lowered Saturday's RH by hand to better match with \nneighbors.",
